\f1\b My read: trust the one-hot columns.
\f0\b0 \
\
  The totals within each CNI backbone agree exactly between Table 1 and the data\
   (cyclosporine total = 23, tacrolimus total = 34), so nothing is missing \'97\
  only the two tacrolimus sub-labels are swapped. The one-hot columns are       \
  patient-level records that were encoded directly from the source file that\
  lives in this repo. Table 1 is a published summary, which could carry a\
  copy/paste or transposition error at the row level without affecting column\
  sums. Patient-level data beats a published marginal count. If it matters, the\
  counts in the data (tacrolimus/MMF = 21, tacrolimus/MTX = 13) are also\
  consistent with the general trend in modern HSCT where MMF has largely\
  replaced MTX as the tacrolimus partner \'97 MTX's mucositis burden makes it less\
  preferred alongside tacrolimus than alongside cyclosporine.\
\
  
\f1\b My proposed mapping:
\f0\b0  cyclosporine=yes & MTX=yes \uc0\u8594  cni-mtx; cyclosporine=yes & \
  MMF=yes \uc0\u8594  cni-mmf; tacrolimus=yes & MTX=yes \u8594  cni-mtx; tacrolimus=yes &\
  MMF=yes \uc0\u8594  cni-mmf. CNI column: cyclosporine/tacrolimus from the respective    \
  indicator. Sirolimus is constant "no" \uc0\u8594  confirm no partner is "other", but\
  since everyone has exactly one of MTX or MMF, this case never fires.\
