\
  I cannot distinguish genuine monotherapy from an unrecorded partner from the\
  source data. The source simply stores the string \cf11 "Cyclosporine\cf2  \cf11 A"\cf2  with no\
  partner field and no free-text notes in the data dictionary. Ingham is an\
  EBMT-registry dataset coded from integer GVHD.Prophylaxis codes (1 =\
  Cyclosporine A; 2 = Cyclosporine + corticosteroids; 7 = Methotrexate +\
  cyclosporine A), so the three levels recorded are the complete registry\
  categories. Code 1 by the EBMT definition is cyclosporine alone \'97 the registry\
  
\f2\i does
\f0\i0  distinguish monotherapy from combination by code \'97 so there is a reasonable\
   argument that it is genuine monotherapy in the source. However, short-course\
  cyclosporine monotherapy is unusual in the era of this cohort, and the EBMT\
  field numbering doesn't guarantee the clinician actually filled in a partner\
  agent rather than leaving it blank.\
\
  
