\cf8 \cb9 \uc0\u10095  \cf10 Add conditioning variables to the harmonized GVHD metadata.\cf2                      \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Follow the "Harmonization Variable Additions" section of CLAUDE.md for all\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 standing conventions.\cf2                                                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 SHAPE: one categorical covariate, one canonical-string covariate, two binaries\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 DEFINITION: Conditioning is the preparative regimen given before graft \cf2          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 infusion,\cf2                                                                        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 and it is the single largest microbiome insult in the transplant course. I want\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 it captured on four separate axes: how intense the regimen was, which cytotoxic\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 drugs it contained, whether it included total body irradiation, and whether it\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 included serotherapy. Splitting irradiation and serotherapy out of the drug\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 string is deliberate \'97 it keeps the drug combinations comparable across studies\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 that record irradiation and serotherapy differently, or not at all.\cf2              \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 CANONICAL VOCABULARY:\cf2                                                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   conditioning_intensity   MAC | RIC | NMA\cf2                                       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     MAC = myeloablative, RIC = reduced-intensity, NMA = non-myeloablative.\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     Where a study records only a two-level myeloablative flag, map 1 -> MAC and\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     0 -> NMA. See NOTES for the consequence of that rule.\cf2                        \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   conditioning_regimen     canonical drug-combination string\cf2                     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     Lower-case drug tokens joined by "/", sorted ALPHABETICALLY so the string \cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 is\cf2                                                                               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     a deterministic join key rather than a clinical-convention name. Token set:\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       bu    busulfan          (DAmico "BU", Ingham X233Bu, Liu "Bu")\cf2             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       cy    cyclophosphamide  (DAmico "EDX", Ingham X270Cyclo, Liu "Cy")\cf2         \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       flu   fludarabine       (DAmico "FLUDARA", Ingham X284.2Fludarab, Liu \cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 "Flu")\cf2                                                                           \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       mel   melphalan         (DAmico "L-PAM", Ingham melphalan dose, Liu \cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 "Mel")\cf2                                                                           \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       thio  thiotepa          (DAmico "TT", Liu "Thio")\cf2                          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       treo  treosulfan        (DAmico "TREO", Liu "Treo")\cf2                        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10       vp16  etoposide         (Ingham VP16 dose)\cf2                                 \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     TBI and serotherapy are NOT tokens in this string \'97 they have their own\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     columns. Strip them out wherever a source embeds them in a regimen name.\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   conditioning_tbi         1/0\cf2                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     1 = total body irradiation included in the preparative regimen.\cf2              \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   conditioning_serotherapy 1/0\cf2                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     1 = ATG or an antibody-based agent (alemtuzumab/rituximab) given as part of\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     conditioning. NA where the study does not record it at all.\cf2                  \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 PLACEMENT: immediately after sample_day_rel_transplant, in the order\cf2             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 conditioning_intensity, conditioning_regimen, conditioning_tbi,\cf2                  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 conditioning_serotherapy. This puts the treatment-exposure block before the \cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 GVHD\cf2                                                                             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 outcome blocks. If the gvhd_prophylaxis columns already exist, conditioning \cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 goes\cf2                                                                             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 before them, since c\cf2                                                             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf8 \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472  \cf31 (107 lines hidden)\cf8  \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 shared by more than one study \'97 cy/flu (all three:\cf2                               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   DAmico 5, Liu 10, Ingham 8), bu/cy/mel (DAmico 24, Ingham 23), flu (Liu 22,\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   Ingham 5), bu/cy (Liu 7, Ingham 12), cy (Liu 3, Ingham 8). If your parse\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   produces materially different overlap, something is wrong \'97 check the token\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   mapping before proceeding.\cf2                                                     \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Before editing anything, read all six study sheets in data_dictionaries.xlsx\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 (the copy in Merging/, which is more current than the one in\cf2                     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Merging/Harmonization/) and cross-tabulate the real source columns in the\cf2        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 *_meta_qiime.tsv files. Two things I want your read on before you write code:\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   1. DAmico intensity. The dictionary labels Conditioning_regimen as\cf2             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      myeloablative, but one of the six regimens is "EDX, FLUDARA, TBI"\cf2           \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      (cyclophosphamide + fludarabine + TBI, n=5 samples), which in adults is\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      commonly reduced-intensity. This is a paediatric cohort so it may \cf2          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 genuinely\cf2                                                                        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      be myeloablative. Check the manuscript methods if you can reach them, and\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      tell me whether to assign MAC to all 104 samples or leave those 5 as NA.\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   2. Liu intensity mapping. Liu uses its own three-tier scale (High /\cf2            \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Intermediate / Low), which is not the ASBMT MAC/RIC/NMA scale Fujimoto\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      uses. My proposed mapping is High -> MAC, Intermediate -> RIC, Low -> NMA.\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Supporting evidence: Low is Flu/TBI (n=22) and Cy/ATG (n=2), and low-dose\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Flu/TBI is the canonical non-myeloablative regimen; Intermediate is\cf2         \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Flu/Cy/TBI, Flu/Cy/Thio/TBI, Flu/Mel and Flu/Treo/TBI, all\cf2                  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      reduced-intensity; High is Bu/Cy and Cy/TBI, classically myeloablative.\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Tell me whether you agree, and flag any case where the regimen string\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      contradicts the intensity label.\cf2                                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 If the data contradicts the spec above, or you hit any of the other\cf2              \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 stop-and-ask triggers in CLAUDE.md, stop and ask me before writing code \'97\cf2        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 report the counts that make it matter and propose a default. Otherwise proceed:\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 edit harmonize_gvhd_metadata.R, extend build_qa() with (a) a coverage row for\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 each new column, (b) a non-canonical value table for conditioning_intensity,\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 (c) a table of every distinct conditioning_regimen string by study so I can\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 eyeball the standardization and see which strings are shared, (d) a check that\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 no conditioning_regimen string contains a "tbi" or "atg" token, and (e) the\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Ingham dose-versus-asserted-intensity cross-check described in NOTES; add unit\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 and end-to-end tests; run the test suite; and append an entry to\cf2                 \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 to_log/harmonization_decisions.md. Do not touch the xlsx.\cf2                        \cb1 \
\
\cf10 \uc0\u9210 \cf2  I'll read all six study sheets and cross-tabulate the relevant source columns\
  before touching any code.\
