\cf8 \cb9 \uc0\u10095  \cf10 Add GVHD prophylaxis to the harmonized GVHD metadata.\cf2                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Follow the "Harmonization Variable Additions" section of CLAUDE.md for all\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 standing conventions.\cf2                                                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 SHAPE: categorical covariate (two columns, two axes)\cf2                             \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 DEFINITION: The pharmacological regimen given to prevent GVHD, started at or\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 around transplant. This is prophylaxis given to everyone as standard of care \'97\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 it is NOT treatment given after GVHD is diagnosed, and the two must not be\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 conflated. Every regimen observed across these studies is a calcineurin\cf2          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 inhibitor backbone plus a partner agent, so I want the partner agent and the\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 backbone identity as separate columns: methotrexate causes mucositis and gut\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 epithelial damage and mycophenolate is enterohepatically recycled, so the\cf2        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 partner agent is the axis most likely to act on the gut microbiome, while\cf2        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 cyclosporine vs tacrolimus is a weaker direct effect I still want recoverable.\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 CANONICAL VOCABULARY:\cf2                                                            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   gvhd_prophylaxis       cni-mtx | cni-mmf | cni-steroid | cni-alone | other\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     cni-mtx      calcineurin inhibitor + methotrexate\cf2                            \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     cni-mmf      calcineurin inhibitor + mycophenolate mofetil\cf2                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     cni-steroid  calcineurin inhibitor + corticosteroids\cf2                         \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     cni-alone    calcineurin inhibitor monotherapy\cf2                               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     other        regimen recorded but composition not specified\cf2                  \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   gvhd_prophylaxis_cni   cyclosporine | tacrolimus\cf2                               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10     NA where the regimen is recorded but the backbone is unspecified.\cf2            \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 PLACEMENT: immediately after sample_day_rel_transplant and before the agvhd\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 block, so the column order reads patient characteristics -> sample timing ->\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 treatment exposure -> outcomes.\cf2                                                  \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 PER-STUDY CONSTRUCTION:\cf2                                                          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Artacho:  not recorded -> NA for both columns. There is no prophylaxis column\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             in the source at all.\cf2                                                \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - DAmico:   not recorded -> NA for both columns. Conditioning_regimen is the\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             PREPARATIVE regimen, not prophylaxis \'97 do not map it. See NOTES.\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Fujimoto: not recorded -> NA for both columns. AGVHD_Treatment is treatment \cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 of\cf2                                                                               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             established aGVHD, not prophylaxis \'97 do not map it. See NOTES.\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Ingham:   gvhd_prophylaxis (3 levels) ->\cf2                                       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "Cyclosporine A + Methotrexate"   -> cni-mtx\cf2                       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "Cyclosporine + Corticosteroids"  -> cni-steroid\cf2                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "Cyclosporine A"                  -> cni-alone\cf2                     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             gvhd_prophylaxis_cni = cyclosporine for all three.\cf2                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             The one row with no clinical metadata stays NA.\cf2                      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Liu2017:  Collapse the five one-hot columns. cyclosporine/tacrolimus give\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             gvhd_prophylaxis_cni; methotrexate/mmf/sirolimus give the partner\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             agent (sirolimus is constant "no" in this cohort). Donor rows -> NA\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             for both columns, as with every other Liu clinical variable.\cf2         \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             Assert in the tests that every recipient has exactly one CNI and\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             exactly one partner agent \'97 this holds in the current data, and a\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             violation means the one-hot expansion has broken.\cf2                    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Vallet:   gvhd_proph_type ->\cf2                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "ciclosporin-MTX"  -> cni-mtx,  cni = cyclosporine\cf2                 \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "cyclosporin-MMF"  -> cni-mmf,  cni = cyclosporine\cf2                 \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10               "Other"            -> other,    cni = NA\cf2                           \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             Note the source spells it "ciclosporin" in one value and\cf2             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10             "cyclosporin" in the other; match both.\cf2                              \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 NOTES:\cf2                                                                           \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Coverage is only 3 of 6 studies (271 of 885 samples). Record the three\cf2         \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   not-recorded studies explicitly in the decision log so the NAs are a logged\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   decision rather than an oversight.\cf2                                             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Two tempting wrong mappings, both of which I want explicitly ruled out in the\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   code comments: DAmico's Conditioning_regimen contains EDX (cyclophosphamide),\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   which is CONDITIONING cyclophosphamide and not post-transplant \cf2                \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 cyclophosphamide\cf2                                                                 \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   prophylaxis; and Fujimoto's AGVHD_Treatment contains mPSL and ATG, which are\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   rescue therapy after aGVHD was diagnosed. Neither belongs in a prophylaxis\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   column.\cf2                                                                        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 - Ingham also has X197ATGmm (ATG given, n=72) and\cf2                                \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   Was.graft.manipulated.for.GVHD.prophylaxis (constant 0). I have deliberately\cf2   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   left both out of this variable \'97 see the stop-and-ask below.\cf2                   \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 Before editing anything, read the Ingham, Liu and Vallet sheets in\cf2               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 data_dictionaries.xlsx (the copy in Merging/, which is more current than the \cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 one\cf2                                                                              \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 in Merging/Harmonization/ and is the only one documenting Ingham's\cf2               \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 gvhd_prophylaxis column) and cross-tabulate the real source columns in the\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 *_meta_qiime.tsv files. I already know of three things to check and want your\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 read on each before you write code:\cf2                                              \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   1. Liu label swap. The dictionary note for Liu's cyclosporine column cites\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      Table 1 as cyclosporine/MTX N=2, cyclosporine/MMF N=21, tacrolimus/MTX\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      N=21, tacrolimus/MMF N=13. The one-hot columns instead give tacrolimus/MMF\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      N=21 and tacrolimus/MTX N=13 \'97 the same multiset, but those two labels\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      swapped. Tell me which you think is authoritative and why.\cf2                  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   2. Ingham ATG. X197ATGmm is described as ATG included in the CONDITIONING\cf2      \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      regimen, but ATG functions as in-vivo T-cell depletion for GVHD\cf2             \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      prophylaxis. Should it be part of this variable, or held back for a future\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      conditioning variable? I lean toward holding it back, since including a\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      single-study column would make gvhd_prophylaxis mean something different\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      for Ingham than for the other two studies.\cf2                                  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   3. Ingham "Cyclosporine A" alone (n=8 samples, 4 patients). Is that genuine\cf2    \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      monotherapy, or a partner agent that went unrecorded? If it cannot be\cf2       \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      distinguished, say so and I will decide whether cni-alone or NA is\cf2          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10      the honest coding.\cf2                                                          \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10   4. Vallet has both cyclosporin and ciclosporin which are different spellings \cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 of the same medication, so just use cyclosporine. \cf2                               \cb1 \
\cb9                                                                                   \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 If the data contradicts the spec above, or you hit any of the other\cf2              \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 stop-and-ask triggers in CLAUDE.md, stop and ask me before writing code \'97\cf2        \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 report the counts that make it matter and propose a default. Otherwise proceed:\cf2  \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 edit harmonize_gvhd_metadata.R, extend build_qa() with a non-canonical value\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 table for both new vocabularies plus a coverage row, add unit and end-to-end\cf2     \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 tests, run the test suite, and append an entry to\cf2                                \cb1 \
\cb9   \cf10 to_log/harmonization_decisions.md. Do not touch the xlsx.\cf2                        \cb1 \
\
