\
  The data dictionary explicitly labels the column "Myeloablative conditioning\
  regimen as a comma-separated list of drug abbreviations" and cites the\
  manuscript's Supplementary Table 2 footnote. The column is described at the\
  study level as myeloablative conditioning \'97 the five Cy/Flu/TBI samples are not\
  singled out as an exception anywhere in the dictionary.\
\
  DAmico is a paediatric cohort (all patients appear to be children, consistent\
  with diagnoses like JMML and the other paediatric-skewed diseases). In\
  paediatric practice the MAC/RIC boundary behaves differently from adult\
  criteria, and Cy/Flu/TBI at institutional paediatric doses is often genuinely\
  myeloablative. I cannot access the manuscript to verify the TBI dose, but\
  without a dose contradiction in the source data there is no evidence to override\
   the dictionary's assertion. I will note the five samples and flag them in the\
  decision log.\
\
