  describes Cy/ATG as "aplastic anemia non-myeloablative conditioning." Flu/TBI at\
   low dose is the canonical Seattle NMA regimen. No contradiction with NMA.\
\
  
\f1\b Flag
\f0\b0 : the Liu paper labels the Low category as "reduced-intensity conditioning,\
  RIC" in the parenthetical in its meaning field. The proposed Low\uc0\u8594 NMA mapping\
  overrides the paper's own label. The regimen evidence makes this the right call\
  \'97 Flu/TBI and Cy/ATG are NMA, not RIC by the ASBMT working definition \'97 but the\
  discrepancy between the paper's label and the mapping should be logged\
  explicitly as a judgement call.\
\
