\
  The regimen evidence is clean:\
\
  - 
\f1\b High
\f0\b0  
\f1\b (n=9)
\f0\b0 : Bu/Cy (7 recipients) \'97 the prototypical MAC regimen \'97 plus\
  Cy/TBI-12Gy (1) and Flu/Cy/TBI-13Gy (1). Twelve-to-thirteen Gy is myeloablative\
  TBI. No contradiction with MAC.\
  - 
\f1\b Intermediate
\f0\b0  
\f1\b (n=24)
\f0\b0 : all Flu-based (Flu/Cy/TBI, Flu/Cy/Thio/TBI, Flu/Mel,\
  Flu/Treo/TBI). Uniformly RIC. No contradiction.\
  - 
\f1\b Low
\f0\b0  
\f1\b (n=24)
\f0\b0 : Flu/TBI (22) and Cy/ATG (2). The data dictionary note itself\
  describes Cy/ATG as "aplastic anemia non-myeloablative conditioning." Flu/TBI at\
   low dose is the canonical Seattle NMA regimen. No contradiction with NMA.\
\
  
\f1\b Flag
\f0\b0 : the Liu paper labels the Low category as "reduced-intensity conditioning,\
  RIC" in the parenthetical in its meaning field. The proposed Low\uc0\u8594 NMA mapping\
  overrides the paper's own label. The regimen evidence makes this the right call\
  \'97 Flu/TBI and Cy/ATG are NMA, not RIC by the ASBMT working definition \'97 but the\
  discrepancy between the paper's label and the mapping should be logged\
  explicitly as a judgement call.\
\
  No case in the regimen-by-intensity cross-tab contradicts the proposed mapping.\
\
  ---\
  Ready to implement as soon as you confirm both reads (or redirect either one).\
