  The totals within each CNI backbone agree exactly between Table 1 and the data\
  (cyclosporine total = 23, tacrolimus total = 34), so nothing is missing \'97 only\
  the two tacrolimus sub-labels are swapped. The one-hot columns are patient-level\
   records that were encoded directly from the source file that lives in this\
  repo. Table 1 is a published summary, which could carry a copy/paste or\
  transposition error at the row level without affecting column sums.\
  Patient-level data beats a published marginal count. If it matters, the counts\
  in the data (tacrolimus/MMF = 21, tacrolimus/MTX = 13) are also consistent with\
  the general trend in modern HSCT where MMF has largely replaced MTX as the\
  tacrolimus partner \'97 MTX's mucositis burden makes it less preferred alongside\
  tacrolimus than alongside cyclosporine.\
\
  
