     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 all four conditioning columns with a code comment.              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  596 +\cf10 - **GOTCHA: transmute() shadowing in Liu and Vallet**: `conditio\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 ning_intensity` and `chemotherapy_regimen` are source column nam\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 es in Liu; `conditioning` is a source column name in Vallet. Loc\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 als are suffixed (`intensity_liu`, `chem_raw_liu`, `src_cond_val\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 let`) to prevent silent shadowing.                              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  597 +\cf10 - **Ingham TBI recovery**: 7 patients (28 samples) have `TBI` = \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 NA but `Irrad` = 0. `Irrad` = 0 means no radiation of any kind w\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 as administered, so TBI must be 0. Recovered with `case_when(!is\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 .na(irrad_ingham) & irrad_ingham == 0L ~ 0L)`. One metadata-less\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10  sample remains NA.                                             \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  598 +\cf10 - **Ingham bu flag**: `X233Bu` = 1 or 2 (both indicate busulfan \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 administration, 2 likely high-dose variant), so the flag is `df[\cf2 \cb1 \
