     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 action) and are recorded here as an open question.              \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  593 +\cf10 - **Liu Low \uc0\u8594  NMA**: The paper's Table 1 labels this group "RIC \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 (low)" parenthetically, but the regimens (Flu/TBI and Cy/ATG) ar\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 e physiologically non-myeloablative. We map Low \uc0\u8594  NMA, overridin\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 g the parenthetical label.                                      \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  594 +\cf10 - **Liu donor rows**: donors are NA for all four conditioning co\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 lumns because `conditioning_intensity`, `chemotherapy_regimen`, \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 and all derived columns are patient-specific. `if_else(donor, NA\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 , ...)` is used for TBI and serotherapy to avoid `!donor & str_d\cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17      +\cf10 etect(...)` returning `"0"` instead of NA for donor rows.       \cf2 \cb1 \
     \cf16 \cb17  595 +\cf10 - **Artacho Myelosuppression**: `Myelosuppression` records a tra\cf2 \cb1 \
